{"t": 1795429888.202414, "kind": "submit", "programmes": ["medicaid", "aca_ptc"], "unknown": [], "hand_off": true, "summary": "Household: 4 people, 2 children, renting, Oregon, two adults working. The income answer was \"between $250 and $300\" with no period or unit; I read it as $250,000-$300,000 a year, which puts the household in the top bracket and makes most programmes unlikely. Asked to clarify twice and got the same answer, so the income figure is unverified. Recommended for application (worth checking): Medicaid and the ACA premium tax credit (marketplace health insurance subsidy). Not recommended at this income: SNAP, WIC, TANF, SSI, CHIP, EITC, child tax credit, free school meals. Assets were not answered. Hand off to a caseworker because the expected cost of mistakes is about $3,400 and the income figure needs confirming. If the income is actually about $25,000 to $30,000 a year, rerun the screening: SNAP, school meals, EITC, child tax credit and CHIP would likely apply.", "asked": ["state", "earned_income", "assets"]}
